# Expected variables. Fill values in a local, gitignored .env. Never commit values.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
GITHUB_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
ARGUS_DATA_DIR=
ARGUS_DRY_RUN=
# Ingestion (optional): the RSS catalog, default config/rss-feeds.json
ARGUS_RSS_FEEDS=
# Google Trends and DexScreener need no key and are on by default. ARGUS_INGEST_STANDING=0 turns both off;
# only the exact string 0 does (false, off, no and empty leave them on).
# The URL overrides exist for tests and local mirrors; leave them unset (empty falls back to the real endpoint).
# ARGUS_INGEST_STANDING=0
# ARGUS_TRENDS_URL=
# ARGUS_DEXSCREENER_URL=
# ARGUS_GITHUB_URL=
# The Meta tick's two trending lists (ADR 0015), same rule: tests and local mirrors only. ARGUS_JUPITER_URL is the whole list prefix and ends in a slash.
# ARGUS_JUPITER_URL=
# ARGUS_GECKOTERMINAL_URL=
# Narrative embedder model (optional; ADR 0007). Cache default ~/.cache/argus/models; `pnpm models:fetch` pre-fetches it.
# ARGUS_MODEL_DIR=
# ARGUS_MODEL_HOST=
# ARGUS_EMBEDDER=hashing is the lexical embedder, for development and tests only
# Judge caps (optional; defaults 10 Narratives per pass, 300 runs and $2 per rolling 24 hours; only news Narratives with at least 2 Signals, and launchpad ones with at least 15, are judged)
# ARGUS_JUDGE_MAX_PER_PASS=
# ARGUS_JUDGE_MAX_RUNS_PER_DAY=
# ARGUS_JUDGE_MIN_SIGNALS=
# ARGUS_JUDGE_MAX_DAILY_USD=
# Propose caps (optional; defaults 3 Narratives per pass, 45 runs per rolling 24 hours, which can be raised or lowered; at most 30 new Proposals a day, which can only be lowered)
# ARGUS_PROPOSE_MAX_PER_PASS=
# ARGUS_PROPOSE_MAX_RUNS_PER_DAY=
# ARGUS_PROPOSE_MAX_NEW_PER_DAY=
# Migrated pump.fun tokens shown to propose as examples (from the Study tables; default 10, at most 20, 0 turns the block off)
# ARGUS_PROPOSE_MIGRATED_EXAMPLES=
# Meta ranking (optional; plain code, no LLM): every ARGUS_META_INTERVAL_MINUTES (1 to 1440, default 15) the worker groups the last 24 h of launches.
# ARGUS_META_RANK_ORDER is a comma list of creators, migrations, migrationsAfter60s, marketCapUsd, tokens (default creators,migrationsAfter60s,marketCapUsd,tokens).
# ARGUS_META_DEX_GROUPS (0 to 50) and ARGUS_META_DEX_CALLS (0 to 60) bound the DexScreener market-cap lookups per run.
# A Meta needs ARGUS_META_MIN_TOKENS (default 5) tokens from ARGUS_META_MIN_CREATORS (default 3) distinct creators in the window, both 1 to 1000.
# A window's hour counts as covered with ARGUS_META_COVERAGE_MIN_CREATES creates (default 10); below ARGUS_META_COVERAGE_NOTE_BELOW (a share, default 0.8) of covered hours
# the War Room says how much data there is, and a thin 24 h window drops the Meta block from the judge and propose prompts.
# ARGUS_META_MIN_TOKENS=
# ARGUS_META_MIN_CREATORS=
# ARGUS_META_COVERAGE_MIN_CREATES=
# ARGUS_META_COVERAGE_NOTE_BELOW=
# ARGUS_META_INTERVAL_MINUTES=
# ARGUS_META_RANK_ORDER=
# ARGUS_META_DEX_GROUPS=
# ARGUS_META_DEX_CALLS=
# What a Meta is (ADR 0014, plain code): a launch theme whose leader token (any age) has a market cap of at least ARGUS_META_ENTER_MCAP_USD (default 1000000) and
# at least ARGUS_META_MIN_COPIES (default 10, 1 to 1000) distinct creators in 24 h; it stays a Meta while the leader holds ARGUS_META_STAY_MCAP_USD (default 500000, not above the
# enter value or both defaults are kept; the copies rule does not apply to staying). Both 1 to 999999999. At most ARGUS_META_MAX_METAS (default 3, 0 to 20) Metas and
# ARGUS_META_WATCHING (default 3, 0 to 20) Watching subjects below the enter cap. Every tick up to ARGUS_META_LEADER_CALLS (default 4, 0 to 20) DexScreener lookups of 30 tokens
# read the leaders' market caps (0 reads none: no new Meta from a trending token, and a Meta or Watching subject whose cap is not read is kept at its last figure, marked stale).
# A figure not read from DexScreener for ARGUS_META_STATE_MAX_MINUTES (default 120, 1 to 10080) ends that carry, however many runs re-saved it; earlier state older than that is not carried either.
# ARGUS_META_ENTER_MCAP_USD=
# ARGUS_META_STAY_MCAP_USD=
# ARGUS_META_MIN_COPIES=
# ARGUS_META_MAX_METAS=
# ARGUS_META_WATCHING=
# ARGUS_META_LEADER_CALLS=
# ARGUS_META_STATE_MAX_MINUTES=
# Top-down leaders (ADR 0015): every Meta tick reads Jupiter's trending list (1 request) and GeckoTerminal's trending pools (3 pages), at most ARGUS_META_TOPDOWN_CALLS
# (default 5, 1 to 10) requests in all, retries included. A token is a leader candidate only when its liquidity is at least ARGUS_META_TOPDOWN_MIN_LIQ_USD (default 50000),
# its market cap is at most ARGUS_META_TOPDOWN_MAX_CAP_LIQ_RATIO (default 100) times its liquidity, and its 24 h volume is at least ARGUS_META_TOPDOWN_MIN_VOLUME_USD
# (default 50000); DexScreener must pass the same tests before a candidate leads (its cap-to-liquidity test also counts the list's liquidity, but only for a token whose Jupiter
# organic score is at least ARGUS_META_TOPDOWN_MIN_ORGANIC, default 50, 0 to 100; a token with no Jupiter score is judged on DexScreener's liquidity alone). Tokenized stocks, quote tokens and generic names are dropped. A subject's copiers
# (ARGUS_META_MIN_COPIES) now count bonk launches as well as pump.fun ones.
# ARGUS_META_TOPDOWN_CALLS=
# ARGUS_META_TOPDOWN_MIN_LIQ_USD=
# ARGUS_META_TOPDOWN_MAX_CAP_LIQ_RATIO=
# ARGUS_META_TOPDOWN_MIN_VOLUME_USD=
# ARGUS_META_TOPDOWN_MIN_ORGANIC=
# Meta summary caps (optional; the one-line summary of the Metas and the Watching subjects, at most 6, a Brain task that counts in the research share; defaults 40 runs and $0.25 per rolling 24 hours)
# ARGUS_META_SUMMARY_MAX_PER_DAY=
# ARGUS_META_SUMMARY_MAX_DAILY_USD=
# Meta grouping (meta redesign ticket 06, ADR 0015): each Meta tick a haiku run groups the trending tokens and the top 30 launch themes into named subjects (reused while
# nothing changed, up to 60 min; counts in the research share). ARGUS_META_GROUP_AI=0 turns it off (subjects are then named by the creators who used a name most);
# ARGUS_META_GROUP_MAX_DAILY_USD is its own cap per rolling 24 hours (default 1.00; a positive number).
# ARGUS_META_GROUP_AI=
# ARGUS_META_GROUP_MAX_DAILY_USD=
# Meme ideas (missed ideas ticket 06, ADR 0013, amended by meta redesign ticket 03): when a subject becomes a Meta, and again every 12 h while it stays one,
# one sonnet run writes 3 meme ideas, stored as meme Proposals that live 12 h. OFF unless ARGUS_MEME_IDEAS=1. ARGUS_MEME_MAX_PER_DAY is the number of runs
# per rolling 24 hours (default 8, at most 40); they count in the research share below. Set it to 8 (or unset it) when upgrading from the old value of 5.
# ARGUS_MEME_IDEAS=
# ARGUS_MEME_MAX_PER_DAY=8
# The Operator's angle on a Meta (ticket 11): requests the War Room accepts in a rolling 24 hours (default 5; this can only lower it, 1 to 5).
# Each angle run also counts in ARGUS_MEME_MAX_PER_DAY and the research share, and waits while ARGUS_MEME_IDEAS is off.
# ARGUS_MEME_ANGLE_MAX_PER_DAY=5
# Moment scanner (moment scanner ticket 01, ADR 0009 as amended 2026-11-19): every ARGUS_MOMENT_INTERVAL_MIN minutes (default 30, at least 15) the worker reads X
# for rising video clips of one topic through the dedicated Argus Chrome profile (ARGUS_CHROME_DIR, default ~/.local/share/argus/chrome) and the War Room lists
# them on /moments. No Claude, no spend. OFF unless ARGUS_MOMENTS=1, which also needs ARGUS_MOMENT_TOPIC: one JSON object with a label, the start time of the
# topic (ISO, ending in Z) and up to 6 spellings. ARGUS_MOMENT_LOADS_PER_DAY can only lower the cap of 100 page loads in a rolling 24 hours.
# ARGUS_MOMENTS=
# ARGUS_MOMENT_TOPIC={"label":"GTA VI","startsAt":"2026-11-19T05:00:00Z","spellings":["GTA VI","GTA 6","GTA6"]}
# ARGUS_MOMENT_INTERVAL_MIN=30
# ARGUS_MOMENT_LOADS_PER_DAY=100
# Research share: judge plus propose (and the Meta summary and meme ideas) may use ARGUS_DAILY_QUOTA_USD x ARGUS_RESEARCH_SHARE of Est. usage in any rolling 24 hours.
# The quota is your estimate of the Est. usage (API-equivalent $) your plan allows per day; defaults $20 and 0.3 ($6)
# ARGUS_DAILY_QUOTA_USD=
# ARGUS_RESEARCH_SHARE=
# API fallback (optional, OFF by default; architecture section 5). When claude -p is rate-limited, judge and propose run on the Anthropic API
# (haiku, REAL money) instead of waiting. The key is read only by the worker, only when ARGUS_API_FALLBACK=1, from here or the environment;
# it is removed from the worker's environment and never reaches claude, Builds or logs. A set-but-empty ANTHROPIC_API_KEY wins over this file.
# ARGUS_API_DAILY_USD can only LOWER the daily real-dollar cap in code ($0.50).
# ARGUS_API_FALLBACK=1
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ARGUS_API_DAILY_USD=
# Helius Free plan key (Phase 3 chain reads: create/migrate times, labels). Read from the environment or this gitignored file, never committed.
HELIUS_API_KEY=
# Launch handoff (optional; ADR 0002). newpairspam's base URL (its `nuxt dev` serves on http://localhost:3000) and a public http(s) logo URL.
# newpairspam's image proxy rejects SVG, so the logo must be a raster image; none is sent when unset.
# ARGUS_NEWPAIRSPAM_URL=
# ARGUS_LAUNCH_LOGO_URL=
# Build containment (optional overrides; the Build token itself lives in ~/.config/argus/build-token, chmod 600, never here)
# ARGUS_PODMAN_BIN is read by the worker and by every script (image:build, verify:contain); image:build still takes the old PODMAN, with a warning.
ARGUS_PODMAN_BIN=
ARGUS_BUILD_IMAGE=
ARGUS_BUILD_TOKEN_FILE=
# Defaults 8 GiB / 4 / 1024 / 2 GiB. /tmp (ARGUS_BUILD_TMP_GIB) plus a fixed 256 MiB /var/tmp and 64 MiB /run may take at most half of the memory cap; a combination beyond that is refused.
ARGUS_BUILD_MEMORY_GIB=
ARGUS_BUILD_CPUS=
ARGUS_BUILD_PIDS=
ARGUS_BUILD_TMP_GIB=
# `pnpm dev:start` also passes any ARGUS_* line in this file to the War Room and the worker (no other keys, no shell expansion).
# A variable already set in the shell wins over .env. The start prints one `env:` line with the key names taken and overridden.
